00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,606
Let us now look closely at the two most important processes.

2
00:00:03,606 --> 00:00:10,833
In an isothermal change, the temperature stays fixed, so P V is constant, which is Boyle's law.

3
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:19,518
In practice it needs thin, highly conducting walls, and a very slow change, so that heat can flow in fast enough.

